  <tei:text>
    <tei:body>
      <tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:haggadah:magid/mah_nishtanah">
        <tei:milestone unit="paragraph" n="1" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:haggadah:magid/mah_nishtanah/1"/>
        <tei:note type="instruction">The youngest person present who is able recites:</tei:note>
        <tei:p>How different this night is from all other nights! On all other nights, we eat both leavened bread and matzah. On this night, [we eat] only matzah. On all other nights, we eat all kinds of herbs. On this night, [we eat] bitter herbs. On all other nights, we do not dip our food even once. On this night, we dip twice. On all other nights, we eat either sitting or reclining. On this night, we all recline.</tei:p>
        <tei:note type="instruction">Keep the matzah uncovered through the next part of the seder. It is appropriate to read and discuss this portion of the Haggadah in a language that those present understand.</tei:note>
      </tei:div>
    </tei:body>
